From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 14:42:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/6] Add regression coverage for the hardened boundaries

Locks in the behaviours the previous commit introduced, so a regression shows up
as a failing test rather than a live vulnerability.

- SSRF guard: private, loopback, link-local, carrier-grade NAT, multicast, IPv6
  unique-local, and IPv4-mapped addresses are refused, including the cloud
  metadata endpoint reached by literal IP and by internal naming convention;
  public addresses still pass, and allow/deny lists are honoured.
- Prompt injection: instruction-override and role-impersonation phrasing is
  defanged, forged trust delimiters are stripped, and ordinary construction text
  passes through byte-identical.
- Tenancy: a workspace path or conversation session id known to two callers
  resolves to different storage for each, across all three memory backends.
- Default-deny: eleven API routes refuse anonymous callers when authentication is
  enabled, the identity header carries no weight in that mode, and discovery and
  probe endpoints stay reachable.

Also fixes a pre-existing fault the tenancy tests surfaced: a missing workspace
path threw, so downloading a file that does not exist returned 500 instead of 404.

Tests: 128 passing, up from 57.
